.TH LIBTLS_TLS_INSTANCE_GET 3 "2023-04-01" "libtls" "TLS Library"
.SH NAME
tls_instance_get - Get TLS instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libtls.h>
.sp
.B tls_instance_t*
.B tls_instance_get(int fd);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B tls_instance_get
function returns a pointer to the TLS instance associated with a file descriptor.
The
.B fd
argument is the file descriptor.
The function returns a pointer to the TLS instance, or 0 if the file descriptor is not associated with a TLS instance.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B tls_instance_get
function to get a pointer to the TLS instance associated with a file descriptor:
.nf
.B #include <libtls.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.sp
.B int main() {
.B   int fd = ...; // Assume a valid file descriptor
.B   tls_instance_t* inst = tls_instance_get(fd);
.B   if(inst == 0) {
.B     fprintf(stderr, "Error getting TLS instance\n");
.B     return 1;
.B   }

.B   // Use the TLS instance

.B   return 0;
.B }
.ne
.fi
